ystem-to-support-timely-decisions0.html" /></ns0:entry><ns0:entry><ns0:title>Canada refocusing Express Entry on top talent that drives economic growth</ns0:title><ns0:id>https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/2026/10/canada-refocusing-express-entry-on-top-talent-that-drives-economic-growth.html</ns0:id><ns0:summary type="html">October 16, 2026—Kitchener, Ontario—Building a stronger Canada means restoring confidence in a well-managed immigration system that meets our economic needs. This includes attracting and retaining skilled talent to complement the Canadian workforce and drive economic growth.</ns0:summary><ns0:author><ns0:name>Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada</ns0:name></ns0:author><ns0:category term="news releases" /><ns0:updated>2026-10-16T11:02:27-04:00</ns0:updated><ns0:link href="https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/2026/10/canada-refocusing-express-entry-on-top-talent-that-drives-economic-growth.html" /></ns0:entry><ns0:entry><ns0:title>Changes to Express Entry for high-wage occupations</ns0:title><ns0:id>https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/2026/10/changes-to-express-entry-for-high-wage-occupations.html</ns0:id><ns0:summary type="html">On November 3, 2026, changes to Express Entry willintroduce points for eligible Canadian work experience or qualifying job offers in high­wage occupations, and remove labour market impact assessment (LMIA) requirements for qualifying job offers used to establish program eligibility and obtain Comprehensive Ranking System (CRS) points</ns0:summary><ns0:author><ns0:name>Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada</ns0:name></ns0:author><ns0:category term="backgrounders" /><ns0:updated>2026-10-16T11:02:13-04:00</ns0:updated><ns0:link href="https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/2026/10/changes-to-express-entry-for-high-wage-occupations.html" /></ns0:entry></ns0:feed>